WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.060
- Okay, get this,

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:05.520
celebrities might not be the
best source of information

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.590
to determine what HIPAA
does and does not do.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:10.423
I know.

00:00:10.423 --> 00:00:12.230
Let's talk about vaccine verification.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.600
That's when someone asks you to prove

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.790
that you've been vaccinated.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.730
Although you might expect
current members of Congress

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.030
to know the law, here's
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.970
getting it completely wrong.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:22.370
- Well, your first question

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.500
is a violation of my HIPAA rights.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.000
You see with HIPAA rights,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.320
we don't have to reveal
our medical records,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.850
and that also involves
our vaccine records.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.520
- And unfortunately, now we have thousands

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.070
of other Marjorie Taylor
Greene's out there,

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.700
all making similar claims.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.840
Here's a guy explaining
that it's a HIPAA violation

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.820
to film a COVID testing site.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.350
- You're not allowed to film.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.470
It's a HIPAA violation.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.030
- [Cameraman] Again?

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:45.867
- It's always been that way.

00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:46.900
- Here's a Karen

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.010
who says she's protected
from wearing a mask

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.800
by the ADA and HIPAA.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.680
- No, I am protected by ADA and HIPAA.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.810
- Here's someone saying the government

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.370
can't ask you about your vaccine status

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.600
because that is illegal on its face.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.790
This person, DotPlusDot, thinks that HIPAA

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.720
might have something to do
with the Hippocratic oath.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.230
And Angela Abarno has some #notlegaladvice

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:07.310
for those of you discussing

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:08.870
whether celebrities are vaccinated.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.010
Quote, you are literally breaking the law

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:13.607
when you post about some
celebrity being vaxxed or not.

00:01:13.607 --> 00:01:15.470
And the idea that someone
might have to prove

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.610
that they have received a vaccine

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.510
has led to some pretty extreme reactions.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:22.010
Quote, "Proposals like these
smack of 1940s Nazi Germany.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:23.700
We must make every effort to keep America

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.310
from becoming a show your papers society."

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:29.520
And that was from freshmen
Representative Madison Cawthorn.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.150
Meanwhile, Libertarian Justin Amash

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.890
called health papers dystopian.

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.020
I guess neither of these gentlemen

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.850
have ever played a sport in school,

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:37.410
because health papers are required,

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.990
or enrolled their children in school,

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:40.930
where health papers are required.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.530
And apparently even pointing
out someone's bad HIPAA takes

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.730
gets you called a Nazi,
like this from Scott Travis.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:48.050
Quote, okay, grammar Nazi.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.190
No one is allowed to ask

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:50.550
for your personal health information

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.420
unless they are HIPAA certified.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.680
That doesn't even make sense.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.570
But these reactions do raise
some interesting legal issues.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:58.200
Does the government
have the power to verify

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.170
whether someone has been vaccinated?

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:02.640
Can employers ask about
someone's vaccine status?

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.534
And what does HIPAA have
to do with any of this?

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:08.200
(triumphant music)

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.033
Hey, Legal Eagles.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:11.970
It's time to think like a
medical malpractice lawyer.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.410
There's a lot of dodgy information

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.737
about vaccine verification, HIPAA,

00:02:14.737 --> 00:02:16.860
and the government's
power over individuals.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.820
So today I'm going to
tackle all of your questions

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:21.070
about COVID-19 and the vaccines,

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.070
starting with everyone's
favorite new law, HIPAA.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:26.380
So what exactly is HIPAA?

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.740
HIPAA, otherwise known as

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.090
the Health Insurance Portability

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.280
and Accountability Act of 1996,

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.901
according to the internet,
is fighting for your freedom.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:34.990
(inspiring music)
She will stop employers

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:36.250
from requiring vaccinations,

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.410
and will vanquish any attempt

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.810
to discuss whether a person is vaccinated.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:43.550
Unfortunately, the reality
is far, far more mundane.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:45.320
To ensure both proper access to

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.320
and confidentiality of medical records,

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:49.690
Congress enacted HIPAA in 1996.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.120
HIPAA is a federal law
that establishes the rules

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.640
for managing medical information

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.720
throughout the United States.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.390
Although states may adopt
stricter confidentiality rules,

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.820
HIPAA sets the minimum standards

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.410
and protections for medical privacy.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.630
HIPAA also gives individuals

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:05.180
control over their own protected
health information, or PHI,

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.220
including their right to access
their PHI and obtain copies,

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.920
request amendments to correct
or complete their records,

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.480
request confidential communications,

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.460
obtain an accounting of who
used or received their PHI,

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.500
impose restrictions on
disclosure of their PHI,

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.620
opt out of fundraising communications,

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.550
and revoke previous authorizations,

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.870
as well as file complaints

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.070
about the misuse of their own PHI.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:27.940
And in 2009, HIPAA was amended

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.670
by the Health Information Technology

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:33.090
for Economic and Clinical
Health Act, or the HITECH Act.

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.380
These amendments, which
became effective in 2013,

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.470
add strict new penalties,

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:39.160
including the possibility of
personal criminal liability,

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.070
and make compliance with HIPAA's privacy

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.850
and security standards
even more important.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:43.980
And I have some bad news

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.590
for all of you freedom fighters out there.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:48.650
HIPAA, signed into law
by MAGA foe Bill Clinton,

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:50.870
is not actually a general privacy law

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.390
protecting anyone from getting
your health information.

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:54.850
HIPAA is a health privacy law

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:56.970
that applies in very limited situations.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.360
And let's get one thing straight

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.720
before we go any further in this video.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:05.720
Attention everyone, it's HIPAA,
H-I-P-A-A, not H-I-P-P-A.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.120
All you have to do is look at the words

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.550
that go into the act.

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:13.180
And it's definitely pronounced
HIPAA, not pronounced HEPA.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:15.520
Okay, sorry, had to get that off my chest.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.310
Now back to what HIPAA
actually is and does.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:20.550
HIPAA includes a privacy
rule that limits doctors,

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.090
hospitals, and health insurance companies

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.540
from disclosing your
personal health information.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:28.200
Now, medical information by
itself is not protected PHI,

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.030
unless it can be related to a person,

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:33.200
that is it contains one or
more individual identifiers.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:36.060
HIPAA specifically applies
to, quote, covered entities,

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.580
which includes healthcare
providers, like I just mentioned,

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.720
clearing houses that
process medical information,

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:41.730
and health plans.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:45.130
And covered entities can't
disclose your PHI to other people

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.750
generally without your permission.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.570
So for example, two employees were fired

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.650
from the University of New Mexico Hospital

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:52.100
when they took cell phone pictures

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.480
of patients receiving treatment

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.500
and then posted those
photos to social media.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.530
And a bunch of people
got fired in LA hospitals

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.980
when they kept accessing celebrities' PHI,

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.730
because, you know, they're celebrities.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.720
Though there are definitely
some exceptions here.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.330
For example, if you're in a car accident,

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.900
paramedics who take you to the hospital

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.110
aren't barred from discussing

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:09.570
your health situation with doctors.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.530
And if the police need
your health information,

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:12.940
there are exceptions allowing them

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:14.270
to get it without your consent.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:17.280
However, HIPAA's privacy rule
doesn't apply to your employer

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.860
if they aren't a covered
entity, and it doesn't apply

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.350
when you voluntarily provide information.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:23.810
Therefore, HIPAA's privacy requirements

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:25.750
don't apply to most private businesses.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:29.010
So for example, when Cowboys'
quarterback Dak Prescott says-

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.740
- I don't necessarily think

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.430
that's exactly important, Clarence.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.263
I think that's HIPAA.

00:05:34.263 --> 00:05:35.950
- He's almost certainly wrong.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:36.783
The HIPAA privacy rule

00:05:36.783 --> 00:05:39.040
probably doesn't apply to your employer.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:41.490
The privacy rule doesn't
protect your employment records,

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:43.820
even if the information in
those records is health-related.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.600
And the NFL is actually a good example

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.770
of how much power employees
have in this context.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:49.350
Think about it, the league has rules

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:51.930
about the way the teams
report player injuries.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.960
Teams have to list
players as questionable,

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:57.020
doubtful, or out because
of injury or illness,

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:59.320
and that's not a HIPAA violation,

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.010
it's an employer work rule.
(team chanting)

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:03.260
And the same goes for everything
related to Aaron Rogers.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.230
But I mean, what can you expect

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.440
for someone that went to Cal?

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:06.280
Go Bruins.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.240
So in most cases, the HIPAA privacy rule

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.670
doesn't apply to the
actions of an employer.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.320
But I can hear you asking the question,

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:14.870
can the government ever make
health papers mandatory?

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.450
And isn't it wrong for the government

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:18.930
to force people to
divulge that information?

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.190
Well, look, I can't tell you

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:23.800
whether things are right or
wrong, I'm just a lawyer.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:24.860
But I'm a lawyer,

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:27.150
I can tell you whether
they're legal or not.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.870
And if you've spent any
time on the internet,

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:30.230
you've probably also heard the claim,

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:32.130
don't ask me about my vaccine status

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.220
or I'll sue, under HIPAA.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:35.053
Well, but many people think

00:06:35.053 --> 00:06:36.300
that sharing personal information

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.780
with government agencies, employers,

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.860
and other third parties
is an invasion of privacy.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:43.380
And look, I mean, that's a
moral question, not a legal one,

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.490
but America doesn't have

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:47.090
one omnibus invasion of privacy law.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.450
If you've ever played high school sports

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.670
or taken a drug test
before starting a new job,

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:53.780
you've experienced this
kind of invasion of privacy

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.060
which requires you to disclose
your personal information

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.470
in order to participate in
something that you want to do.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:00.160
And here's an incomplete
list of activities

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:01.910
that you can only participate in

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:03.940
by giving up your private information.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.750
A driver's license, a hunting license,

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.040
concealed carry permit,
school vaccinations,

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:10.160
sports physicals, international travel,

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.070
immigration, and voting.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:14.220
Of course, those with law
degrees from twitter.com

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:15.930
will say that those records are provided

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:19.400
totally voluntarily, a
vaccine verification is not.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.090
But in the eyes of the law,
they're exactly the same thing.

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:24.180
You don't have to provide
your kid's vaccination records

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:26.570
if you don't want to, but
if the school requires them,

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:27.403
that means your kids

00:07:27.403 --> 00:07:29.320
don't get to be enrolled in that school.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:30.530
Likewise, you might prefer

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:32.050
not to provide personal information

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:35.190
demonstrating that you should
get a concealed carry permit,

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:37.090
but you don't have to provide it.

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:38.120
You might not want your employer

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.320
to know whether you've done drugs or not,

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:43.220
but sometimes that's a
condition of employment.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:45.820
And really, there are a lot
of instances when employers

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:49.220
can and probably should
be asking about things

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:51.350
that might be considered
health information.

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:53.220
A person might volunteer that information

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:55.450
when they call in sick, or
mention it to a coworker,

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:57.340
or the person might write
the information down

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:59.680
on a workers' compensation
form after an injury,

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.900
or fill out a health insurance
form to receive benefits.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:02.910
And there are plenty of state laws

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.490
requiring you to provide medical records

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:06.130
to receive workers' compensation,

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.860
and if you choose not to
provide this information

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:08.820
to your employer,

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.660
the employer can generally
discipline or fire you.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:14.300
Remember, in the US, most
employment is at will.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.080
And with respect to COVID-19 vaccines,

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:19.680
President Biden has requested
OSHA begin promulgating rules

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.670
about vaccines in the workplace,

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:23.440
and it may be the case that employers

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.770
are actually creating an
unsafe work environment

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:29.120
by allowing the
unvaccinated to go to work.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.540
But what about other laws?

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.040
Well, generally private businesses

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.360
can have any rules they want,

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.900
so long as they don't discriminate.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:36.730
Now, of course, businesses
still can't discriminate

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:38.290
against protected classes.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.420
Businesses still have to follow Title VII,

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:41.760
the Americans with Disabilities Act,

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.730
and other laws barring discrimination.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:45.300
It's illegal to refuse to serve someone

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.260
based on their race, religion,
sex, or national origin.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:49.700
However, someone's vaccine status

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.750
doesn't fall into any of
those protected categories.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:54.660
Being unvaccinated or vaccinated

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:56.360
is not considered a disability.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.440
The ADA does regulate medical examinations

00:08:58.440 --> 00:08:59.400
in the workplace, though.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.840
Under the ADA, an employer
can't ask a job applicant

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:02.940
whether they have a disability

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:05.100
or about the nature of
an obvious disability.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.550
The employer also can't force someone

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:09.090
to pass a medical examination
before being offered the job.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:11.040
However, after the person
is offered the job,

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.880
an employer can condition the job offer

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.950
on passing a medical examination.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.340
But there are some caveats here.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:19.640
The employer can't impose a
medical exam on just one person.

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:20.560
For it to be legal,

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.890
all employees in the job
have to take the medical exam

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.530
and it has to be related to
the requirements of the job.

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:26.770
But there are some new state laws

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:28.360
that are attempting to
change the status quo

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:29.420
on medical information.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.520
In Florida, for example,
businesses are not allowed

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:33.950
to make their own decisions
when it comes to COVID.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:35.420
Governor DeSantis signed an order

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.150
stating that the airlines and cruise ships

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:39.090
could not demand proof of vaccination

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.110
anywhere in the travel-friendly state.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:41.943
So the question is,

00:09:41.943 --> 00:09:43.540
can an employer discriminate
against a person

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.120
for not taking the vaccine?

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.420
And the answer is probably yes,

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:47.980
but it depends on the context.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.930
The EEOC issued interim guidelines

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:51.890
saying that employers may encourage

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:54.390
or possibly require COVID-19 vaccinations,

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:55.420
but they still must comply

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:56.870
with the Americans with Disabilities Act,

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:59.220
Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964,

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.470
and other workplace laws.

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:03.080
So yes, subject to certain exceptions,

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:05.830
an employer can make a
COVID vaccine mandatory,

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.730
but they can't physically restrain you

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:08.730
and jab you in the arm,

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.970
but they can offer you a
carrot, like a $100 bonus,

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:15.280
or a stick, in other words,
getting fired if you refuse.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:17.450
And if your employer wants
these specific results,

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.410
they could ask you to
voluntarily turn them over,

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:20.760
or make you sign a HIPAA waiver

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.620
so they can get the
results from a third party,

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.670
because remember, HIPAA
does actually apply

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:25.800
to healthcare providers

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:27.670
and their disclosures to third parties.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:29.880
And on the flip side, it's
probably legal for employers

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:32.020
to ban vaccinated people as well,

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:34.260
though that might be subject
to the OSHA requirements

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:35.110
we talked about earlier

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:38.720
where if an employer is creating
an unsafe work environment,

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:41.040
well, they run into liability
on that end as well.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.170
But a private school in Florida

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:44.330
banned teachers who had been vaccinated

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.500
from any in-person contact with students,

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.440
citing debunked conspiracy theories

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:49.820
about vaccine side effects.

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:51.430
The school's assessment
about vaccine safety

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:54.170
is completely contradicted
by science and data,

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.780
but the school probably has
a right to make its own rules

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:58.140
since it's not public.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:10:59.560
And in keeping with the reality of HIPAA

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.540
that it isn't a general privacy law,

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:03.080
this school's requirement

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:06.400
for staff to fill out a form
disclosing their vaccine status

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:07.930
probably passes muster.

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:08.763
So as you can see,

00:11:08.763 --> 00:11:11.440
there's freedom of choice
going in both directions.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.273
But of course,

00:11:12.273 --> 00:11:14.460
what about the Supreme
Court and government action?

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:16.290
Lots of people seem to
think that the Supreme Court

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:17.660
should immediately strike down any law

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:19.530
that resembles a vaccine passport,

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:22.600
but a vaccine passport is
just an immunization record,

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.450
and immunization records are legal,

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.630
and the Supreme Court has
already weighed in on it.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:27.730
So in terms of whether the government

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:30.410
can make vaccines mandatory
just like employers,

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.990
the answer is probably yes,

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:34.060
but there are also many, many caveats.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:34.930
The landmark case on this

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:36.350
is called Jacobson v. Massachusetts,

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:38.460
which we've talked about
many times on this channel,

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:41.210
but a short summary,
during a smallpox outbreak

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:43.520
in Cambridge, Massachusetts in 1902,

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:45.780
the state introduced an
ordinance requiring all adults

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:48.840
to be vaccinated or
revaccinated against smallpox.

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:51.170
The penalty for non-compliance
was a $5.00 fine.

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:53.060
And the man named Jacobson
refused the vaccine,

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.850
saying it violated his religious liberty.

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:57.340
Now, states generally have the
right to regulate the health,

00:11:57.340 --> 00:12:00.140
safety, welfare, and
morals of its citizen.

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:01.590
These are known as police powers.

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.370
However, these powers have been balanced

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:04.820
with individual liberty interests.

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:06.820
And the question was
whether the US Constitution

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:09.510
prevented the state from
implementing vaccines.

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:11.930
The Supreme Court held
that the Constitution

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:14.670
did not prevent such a law
from going into effect.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.110
That effectively, the public interest

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:17.930
in making sure everyone was vaccinated

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:21.140
overrode the personal liberties
in this particular case.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:24.010
Now, Jacobson was decided in 1905.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.630
This is a case involving a state law,

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.760
but it's likely that the
same result would be reached

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.640
with respect to the
federal government as well,

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:33.210
so long as the federal government
has the power in question.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:35.770
Remember, the federal government
is theoretically limited

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.510
more than a state government is.

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:39.540
If the federal government has that power,

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:41.770
then it's likely that the Constitution

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:44.690
isn't going to prevent such
a law from going into effect.

00:12:44.690 --> 00:12:47.460
And then some people are
pointing to the Nuremberg Code

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:50.439
as something that would
prevent a vaccine mandate

00:12:50.439 --> 00:12:52.830
or a vaccine passport.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:56.673
The Nuremberg Code, which is not a US law,

00:12:57.570 --> 00:13:00.480
no, that's probably not going
to prevent the government

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:02.910
from implementing any of those laws.

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:04.980
But on a slightly more reasonable note,

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:06.270
there is the question of whether HIPAA

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:08.620
overrules the vaccine mandate.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.330
And there is an argument
that HIPAA prevents

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:12.740
vaccine mandates and vaccine passports.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:14.990
It's wrong, but there is an argument.

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:15.823
The argument goes

00:13:15.823 --> 00:13:17.460
that it would be illegal
to mandate a vaccine,

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:19.010
because doing so requires the government

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:20.800
to find out who has been vaccinated.

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:21.930
Under this view of the law,

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:24.730
vaccine cards would also be
illegal because of HIPAA,

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:27.790
because the vaccine
card is a health record,

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:30.970
but that's a pretty incorrect
interpretation of HIPAA.

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:32.810
As we discussed, the law
prohibits the release

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:34.330
of protected health information

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:36.650
by covered entities without your consent.

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:38.650
Who are these covered entities again?

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:39.860
Well, healthcare providers,

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:42.130
health insurers, and
medical billing companies.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:43.340
What do they have to do?

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.300
Well, they have to keep your
information confidential,

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:46.650
safeguard it against security threats,

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:47.530
and make sure employees

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:48.970
know how to protect your information.

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:50.550
So unless you work for a health provider

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:51.470
or an insurance company

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:54.290
and you are a patient and
client of that company

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:55.340
at the same time,

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:57.940
your employer probably
isn't constrained by HIPAA,

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.480
and neither is the government.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:00.700
And even healthcare providers

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:03.800
have the right to ask their
staff about their vaccine status

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:05.620
since they are requesting the information,

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:08.000
they're not releasing it to a third party.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.110
So the bottom line is that
HIPAA means health providers

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:11.530
can't release your information about you

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:12.550
without your permission.

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:14.830
The law says nothing about
whether you can or should

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.790
answer questions about
your vaccination status

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:17.990
or other health issues.

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:18.823
HIPAA doesn't apply

00:14:18.823 --> 00:14:21.630
when you are talking
about your own health.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.650
And of course, HIPAA has
all kinds of exceptions

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:25.670
carved out in the law itself.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:28.150
So even if HIPAA applied, the
only thing you'd need to do

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:30.700
to create another exception is pass a law,

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:33.570
the same law that probably
requires the vaccination

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.800
or vaccination status itself.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:38.240
But whether you're staying
home to avoid the anti-vaxxers

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:40.950
